"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"icon\"\n    xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"\u003e\u003c!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) --\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M433.941 65.941l-51.882-51.882A48 48 0 0 0 348.118 0H176c-26.51 0-48 21.49-48 48v48H48c-26.51 0-48 21.49-48 48v320c0 26.51 21.49 48 48 48h224c26.51 0 48-21.49 48-48v-48h80c26.51 0 48-21.49 48-48V99.882a48 48 0 0 0-14.059-33.941zM266 464H54a6 6 0 0 1-6-6V150a6 6 0 0 1 6-6h74v224c0 26.51 21.49 48 48 48h96v42a6 6 0 0 1-6 6zm128-96H182a6 6 0 0 1-6-6V54a6 6 0 0 1 6-6h106v88c0 13.255 10.745 24 24 24h88v202a6 6 0 0 1-6 6zm6-256h-64V48h9.632c1.591 0 3.117.632 4.243 1.757l48.368 48.368a6 6 0 0 1 1.757 4.243V112z\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n          \u003cspan class=\"check-icon tw-hidden\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"icon\"\n    xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"\u003e\u003c!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) --\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M173.898 439.404l-166.4-166.4c-9.997-9.997-9.997-26.206 0-36.204l36.203-36.204c9.997-9.998 26.207-9.998 36.204 0L192 312.69 432.095 72.596c9.997-9.997 26.207-9.997 36.204 0l36.203 36.204c9.997 9.997 9.997 26.206 0 36.204l-294.4 294.401c-9.998 9.997-26.207 9.997-36.204-.001z\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003c/button\u003e\n        \n      \u003cbutton \n        class=\"\n          tw-select-none \n          tw-mx-2 \n          tw-block \n          group-[.is-open]:tw-hidden \n          print:!tw-hidden\" \n        disabled\n        aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"icon\"\n    xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"\u003e\u003c!-- Font Awesome Free 5.15.4 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license/free (Icons: CC BY 4.0, Fonts: SIL OFL 1.1, Code: MIT License) --\u003e\u003cpath d=\"M328 256c0 39.8-32.2 72-72 72s-72-32.2-72-72 32.2-72 72-72 72 32.2 72 72zm104-72c-39.8 0-72 32.2-72 72s32.2 72 72 72 72-32.2 72-72-32.2-72-72-72zm-352 0c-39.8 0-72 32.2-72 72s32.2 72 72 72 72-32.2 72-72-32.2-72-72-72z\"/\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/button\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n  \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"tw-block tw-m-0 tw-p-0\"\u003e\u003ccode \n    id=\"codeblock-id-6\" \n    class=\"\n      chroma \n      !tw-block \n      tw-p-0\n      tw-m-0\n      tw-transition-[max-height] \n      tw-duration-500 \n      tw-ease-in-out \n      group-[.is-closed]:!tw-max-h-0 \n      group-[.is-wrap]:tw-text-wrap\n      tw-overflow-y-hidden\n      tw-overflow-x-auto\n      tw-scrollbar-thin\n      \"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u0026lt;Internal Thinking\u0026gt;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e{Complex_CoT}\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u0026lt;/Internal Thinking\u0026gt;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u0026lt;Question\u0026gt;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e{Question}\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u0026lt;/Question\u0026gt;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eThe \u0026lt;Internal Thinking\u0026gt; represents your internal thoughts about the \u0026lt;Question\u0026gt;. Based on this, generate a rich and high-quality final response to the user. If there is a clear answer, provide it first. Ensure your final response closely follows the \u0026lt;Question\u0026gt;. The response style should resemble GPT-4’s style as much as possible. Output only your final response, without any additional content.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinally, the authors extracted 20k Data Samples from the original 40k Data Samples (Question-Answer Pairs) and performed the above process. Therefore, there are currently 20k (Question, Complex Rationale, Response) Tuples, and 20k (Question, Answer) Pairs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 id=\"huatuogpt-o1-3-step-supervised-fine-tuning\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#huatuogpt-o1-3-step-supervised-fine-tuning\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e21 HuatuoGPT-o1 #3 Step: Supervised Fine-Tuning\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe purpose of this step is to train the LLM to first output the Long Chain-of-Thought Style Rationale, and then get the final Response. Therefore, this stage is mainly based on the 20k (Question, Complex Rationale, Response) Tuples. The input to the LLM is the Question, and the output is Complex Rationale + Response.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 id=\"huatuogpt-o1-4-step-reinforcement-learning\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#huatuogpt-o1-4-step-reinforcement-learning\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e22 HuatuoGPT-o1 #4 Step: Reinforcement Learning\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo further optimize the model\u0026rsquo;s reasoning ability, the authors also trained the model using the remaining 20k (Question, Answer) Pairs combined with PPO.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRegarding the calculation of Reward, it is mainly determined by comparing the LLM\u0026rsquo;s Output and the Ground-truth Answer through a Verifier:\n\u003cfigure\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightgallery\" href=\"/paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/raward_function.png\" title=\"\" data-thumbnail=\"/paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/raward_function.png\" data-sub-html=\"\u003ch2\u003eReward Function in HuatuoGPT-o1\u003c/h2\u003e\"\u003e\u003cimg  loading=\"lazy\" src='/paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/raward_function.png' srcset=\"/paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/raward_function_hu_fcde2733edbceff9.webp 800w, /paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/raward_function_hu_d1f53b0421f10dc8.webp 1200w, /paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/raward_function_hu_7a2db94b5eb4e215.webp 1600w\"   height=\"174\" width=\"804\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"image-caption\"\u003eReward Function in HuatuoGPT-o1\u003c/figcaption\u003e\n    \u003c/figure\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat\u0026rsquo;s more interesting is that, if the LLM deduces a wrong answer, it will still receive a Positive Reward (just a smaller one), but when the LLM\u0026rsquo;s Output does not follow the Think-before-Answering behavior pattern, it will not receive any Reward. To ensure stable learning under Sparse Reward, KL Divergence is also added to the final Reward Function to prevent updates from deviating too much from the Initial Policy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 id=\"experimental-performance-of-huatuogpt-o1\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#experimental-performance-of-huatuogpt-o1\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e23 Experimental Performance of HuatuoGPT-o1\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eRegarding the details of model training, the authors trained HuatuoGPT-o1-8B and 70B based on Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct and 70B. It is worth noting that the LR for SFT in Stage 1 was set to only 5e-6 and the LR for RL in Stage 2 was set to only 5e-7. From the table below, Table 1, it can also be seen that HuatuoGPT performs better than the Baseline.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cfigure\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightgallery\" href=\"/paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/table-1.png\" title=\"\" data-thumbnail=\"/paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/table-1.png\" data-sub-html=\"\u003ch2\u003eTable 1: Main Results on Medical Benchmarks. LLMs with \u0026lsquo;capsule\u0026rsquo; emoji are specifically trained for the medical domain, and indicates LLMs training for long chain-of-thought reasoning. \u0026lsquo;w/o\u0026rsquo; means \u0026lsquo;without\u0026rsquo;. Within each segment, bold highlights the best scores, and underlines indicate the second-best.\u003c/h2\u003e\"\u003e\u003cimg  loading=\"lazy\" src='/paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/table-1.png' srcset=\"/paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/table-1_hu_825c520f91daa609.webp 800w, /paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/table-1_hu_163325e43e6158a7.webp 1200w, /paper-intro/huatuogpt-o1-towards-medical-complex-reasoning-with-llms/table-1_hu_e77f51e4355ece05.webp 1600w\"   height=\"651\" width=\"1024\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption class=\"image-caption\"\u003eTable 1: Main Results on Medical Benchmarks. LLMs with \u0026lsquo;capsule\u0026rsquo; emoji are specifically trained for the medical domain, and indicates LLMs training for long chain-of-thought reasoning. \u0026lsquo;w/o\u0026rsquo; means \u0026lsquo;without\u0026rsquo;. Within each segment, bold highlights the best scores, and underlines indicate the second-best.\u003c/figcaption\u003e\n    \u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003ch2 id=\"conclusion\" class=\"headerLink\"\u003e\n    \u003ca href=\"#conclusion\" class=\"header-mark\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e24 Conclusion\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis article shared \u003ca href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.18925\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eHuatuoGPT-o1, Towards Medical Complex Reasoning with LLMs (2024/12)\u003c/a\u003e — an o1 model specifically for the Medical Domain. After reading about HuatuoGPT-o1, we were able to learn how to train an o1 model in the Medical Domain. I feel that what we learned the most from this paper is how to build a Domain-Specific o1 model from scratch in a relatively low-cost way (compared to OpenAI o1). This includes how to design the overall process (Dataset Collection, Preprocess, Transformation, SFT, RL), and how to write the Prompts (Search Strategy, CoT Trajectory to Complex CoT).\u003c/p\u003e",
        "language": "en"
    },
    ]
}
